A||||3||PJ||Remote Oil Filter Location?||||1||
Z||000000||PJ||01-06-2001||11:04 PM||||Anyone here relocated the oil filter on their ride? If so, where'd you put it? The sandwich plate I'm using on the block has a bypass so all the oil doesn't go to the cooler up front and the temp runs high. I'm leaning towards using the rear storage compartment but don't want to spend more money on braided hose if I don't have to.   ||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||01-07-2001||03:18 PM||||Why not next to the vapor can? There's plenty of room in that corner for things. Less on a V6 but should still fit a filter.||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||01-07-2001||06:57 PM||||My filter is mounted on the right side of the cradle. I did add a shield over it. I had to do this on the 3800 swap. I kept it low so it wouldn't drain back into the engine.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 01-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero_Freak||01-08-2001||01:22 AM||||  I still have the 2.8, but I did the same as TerryK.  Right in front of the right rear tire.  Works great, doesn't drain back and doesn't make a mess when draining.  That alone is worth the $40 for the kit.  I hated trying to keep the back of the block clean.||||reg||1
